<% content_for :title, "On Jobs | Bipolar Sober" %>

<main class="toolbox-jobs-page">

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="toolbox-jobs-hero">
    <div class="toolbox-jobs-hero-content">

      <p class="toolbox-jobs-eyebrow">
        BIPOLAR SOBER / TOOLBOX / ON JOBS
      </p>

      <h1>
        <span>YOU ARE</span>
        <span>NOT YOUR</span>
        <span>FUCKING JOB.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="toolbox-jobs-intro">
        EMPLOYED. UNEMPLOYED.<br>
        REJECTED. STARTING OVER.<br>
        STILL FUCKING YOU.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- WORK + IDENTITY -->
  <section class="jobs-section jobs-section-pink">

    <div class="jobs-section-number">
      01 / WORK + IDENTITY
    </div>

    <div class="jobs-section-content">

      <h2>
        WHAT YOU DO<br>
        ISN'T WHO<br>
        YOU ARE.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Jobs make it ridiculously easy to confuse occupation with identity.
        One of the first questions people ask is, "What do you do?"
      </p>

      <p>
        So when you're unemployed, changing careers, struggling at work,
        or starting over, it can feel like you lost more than a paycheck.
        It can feel like you lost an answer to who you are.
      </p>

      <div class="jobs-callout">
        <p>
          A JOB CAN BE PART OF YOUR LIFE.<br>
          IT DOESN'T GET TO BE THE DEFINITION OF IT.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- UNEMPLOYMENT -->
  <section class="jobs-section jobs-section-yellow">

    <div class="jobs-section-number">
      02 / UNEMPLOYMENT
    </div>

    <div class="jobs-section-content">

      <h2>
        NO JOB<br>
        DOESN'T MEAN<br>
        NO VALUE.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Unemployment can mess with routine, confidence, money,
        social connection, and your sense of forward movement.
      </p>

      <p>
        And after enough time, your brain may start turning a temporary
        situation into a statement about your entire fucking existence.
      </p>

      <div class="jobs-before-after">

        <div>
          <p class="jobs-label">THE STORY</p>
          <p>I DON'T HAVE A JOB, SO I'M FAILING AT LIFE.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p class="jobs-label">THE FACT</p>
          <p>I DON'T HAVE A JOB RIGHT NOW.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <p>
        Those are not the same sentence.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- REJECTION -->
  <section class="jobs-section jobs-section-purple">

    <div class="jobs-section-number">
      03 / REJECTION
    </div>

    <div class="jobs-section-content">

      <h2>
        THANKS,<br>
        BUT NO<br>
        FUCKING THANKS.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Applications disappear. Interviews go nowhere.
        Somebody else gets picked. Sometimes you never even get
        the courtesy of knowing why.
      </p>

      <p>
        Rejection hurts. But your brain loves taking one company's
        decision and turning it into a universal verdict.
      </p>

      <div class="jobs-question">
        DID THEY REJECT ME<br>
        FOR THIS JOB —<br>
        OR DID MY BRAIN DECIDE<br>
        THEY REJECTED ME AS A PERSON?
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- COMPARISON -->
  <section class="jobs-section jobs-section-black">

    <div class="jobs-section-number">
      04 / COMPARISON
    </div>

    <div class="jobs-section-content">

      <h2>
        EVERYBODY<br>
        ELSE LOOKS<br>
        AHEAD.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Somebody has the title. Somebody has the salary.
        Somebody bought the house. Somebody got promoted.
        Somebody's career looks beautifully linear from the outside.
      </p>

      <p>
        You usually don't see their whole life.
        You see the résumé version.
      </p>

      <div class="jobs-callout">
        <p>
          SOMEBODY ELSE'S TIMELINE<br>
          IS NOT YOUR DEADLINE.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- STARTING OVER -->
  <section class="jobs-section jobs-section-pink">

    <div class="jobs-section-number">
      05 / STARTING OVER
    </div>

    <div class="jobs-section-content">

      <h2>
        BACK TO<br>
        FUCKING<br>
        SQUARE ONE?
      </h2>

      <p>
        Starting over can feel humiliating when you think you were
        supposed to be further along by now.
      </p>

      <p>
        But starting over doesn't mean everything that came before
        disappeared.
      </p>

      <div class="jobs-list">

        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <p>You still have what you learned.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <p>You still have skills you built.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <p>You still know what didn't work.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <p>You know more about what you actually need.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>05</span>
          <p>You are not starting from zero. You're starting from experience.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- RECOVERY -->
  <section class="jobs-section jobs-section-yellow">

    <div class="jobs-section-number">
      06 / RECOVERY
    </div>

    <div class="jobs-section-content">

      <h2>
        YOUR LIFE<br>
        MAY HAVE<br>
        OTHER PRIORITIES.
      </h2>

      <p>
        There are times when staying stable, staying sober,
        taking care of yourself, rebuilding routines, or simply getting
        through the day may need more attention than climbing some
        imaginary professional ladder.
      </p>

      <p>
        That doesn't mean ambition disappeared.
        It means your priorities may need to exist in an order that
        actually keeps your life functioning.
      </p>

      <div class="jobs-callout">
        <p>
          SURVIVAL IS NOT<br>
          A FUCKING CAREER GAP.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- BIPOLAR + WORK -->
  <section class="jobs-section jobs-section-purple">

    <div class="jobs-section-number">
      07 / BIPOLAR + WORK
    </div>

    <div class="jobs-section-content">

      <h2>
        YOUR BRAIN<br>
        DOESN'T CLOCK<br>
        OUT AT FIVE.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Mood episodes can affect energy, concentration, sleep,
        motivation, judgment, communication, and your ability to
        function consistently at work.
      </p>

      <p>
        That can make work complicated in ways that aren't always
        visible to coworkers, managers, or even you until things
        start going sideways.
      </p>

      <div class="jobs-list">

        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <p>Pay attention when sleep starts changing.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <p>Notice sudden changes in energy or productivity.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <p>Watch for unusually big commitments or impulsive decisions.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <p>Notice when depression makes ordinary tasks feel impossible.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>05</span>
          <p>Use your treatment and support system when mood symptoms start changing.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- THE SEARCH -->
  <section class="jobs-section jobs-section-black">

    <div class="jobs-section-number">
      08 / THE JOB SEARCH
    </div>

    <div class="jobs-section-content">

      <h2>
        MAKE THE<br>
        SEARCH A JOB.<br>
        NOT YOUR LIFE.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Job hunting can expand until every hour becomes another opportunity
        to refresh listings, rewrite something, compare yourself to strangers,
        or wonder why nobody has emailed you back.
      </p>

      <p>
        Give the search boundaries.
      </p>

      <div class="jobs-list">

        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <p>Choose specific times to search and apply.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <p>Set a realistic application goal instead of endlessly scrolling.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <p>Track applications somewhere outside your head.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <p>Stop when the work you've planned for the day is done.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>05</span>
          <p>Do something afterward that has absolutely nothing to do with employment.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- CONTROL -->
  <section class="jobs-section jobs-section-pink">

    <div class="jobs-section-number">
      09 / WHAT'S YOURS?
    </div>

    <div class="jobs-section-content">

      <h2>
        DO YOUR PART.<br>
        DROP THE<br>
        REST.
      </h2>

      <div class="jobs-control-grid">

        <div>
          <p class="jobs-label">YOURS</p>

          <p>Your résumé.</p>
          <p>Your application.</p>
          <p>Your preparation.</p>
          <p>Your effort.</p>
          <p>Your follow-up.</p>
          <p>Your next move.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p class="jobs-label">NOT YOURS</p>

          <p>The applicant pool.</p>
          <p>The hiring manager's preferences.</p>
          <p>Internal candidates.</p>
          <p>Budget changes.</p>
          <p>Whether somebody responds.</p>
          <p>The final decision.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <p>
        Do the part that's yours.
        Don't spend the rest of the day trying to mentally control
        shit you literally cannot control.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- BAD DAY -->
  <section class="jobs-section jobs-section-yellow">

    <div class="jobs-section-number">
      10 / WHEN IT HURTS
    </div>

    <div class="jobs-section-content">

      <h2>
        YOU GOT<br>
        REJECTED.<br>
        NOW WHAT?
      </h2>

      <div class="jobs-list">

        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <p>Be pissed off if you're pissed off.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <p>Don't immediately turn disappointment into a judgment about yourself.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <p>Take whatever useful information exists.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <p>Leave behind the shit you can't know.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>05</span>
          <p>Apply for the next fucking job.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- ENDING -->
  <section class="jobs-ending">

    <p class="jobs-ending-small">
      YOUR PAYCHECK IS NOT A MEASUREMENT OF YOUR HUMAN WORTH.
    </p>

    <h2>
      YOU ARE<br>
      MORE THAN<br>
      YOUR RÉSUMÉ.
    </h2>

    <p>
      Build the career. Change the career. Lose the job.
      Find another one. Start again if you have to.
      You are still the person living the life around it.
    </p>

    <%= link_to "← BACK TO TOOLBOX",
        toolbox_path,
        class: "jobs-back-link" %>

  </section>

</main>